.TH tusize n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tusize
.PP
A small \fBdu\fR: recursive byte totals and human\-readable formatting. Symlinks are not followed: a link counts with its own size (\fBfile lstat\fR, on Unix the length of the target path), so cyclic links cannot loop.
.SS Commands
.TS
l l.
Command	Result
\fBbytes path\fR	size of a file, or recursive total of a directory (incl. dotfiles)
\fBhuman n ?\-si 0|1?\fR	human\-readable size; binary units (KiB ... YiB) by default, decimal (kB ... YB) with \fB\-si 1\fR
\fBentries dir\fR	list of \fB{bytes path}\fR for each immediate child, sorted by path
.TE
.CS
package require tclutils::tusize
tusize::bytes   ./project          ;# 1048576
tusize::human   1536               ;# 1.5 KiB
tusize::human   1500 -si 1         ;# 1.5 kB
tusize::entries ./project          ;# {4096 ./project/docs} {2048 ./project/src} ...
.CE
.PP
The unit always names its base: \fBKiB\fR is 1024, \fBkB\fR is 1000. 1500 and 1536 bytes are both \fB1.5 KiB\fR because one decimal is shown; \fBtunumfmt::toHuman\fR writes the bare \fBK\fR for 1000 (\fB1.5K\fR), like \fBnumfmt\fR.
.PP
Errors use \fB{TCLUTILS TUSIZE ...}\fR (\fBNOTFOUND\fR, \fBNOTDIR\fR, \fBVALUE\fR).
